  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "value": "Expressed in testis, ovary, small intestine, prostate, lung, liver, kidney and leukocytes"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "value": "Expressed from 16 dpc in ovary and testis and during P6-P16 during differentiation of ovarian follicles"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"
      }
     ],
     "value": "The DAD domain regulates activation via by an autoinhibitory interaction with the GBD/FH3 domain. This autoinhibition is released upon competitive binding of an activated GTPase. The release of DAD allows the FH2 domain to then nucleate and elongate nonbranched actin filaments (By similarity)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "DOMAIN"
  },
